<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:0}h2{font-size:15px;margin:0 0 8px}
p{margin:0 0 10px}code{font:12px Menlo,monospace}</style>
</head><body>
<h2>Geant4 @VERSION@ is installed</h2>
<p>It is in <code>@PREFIX@</code>, and the datasets that were selected are in
<code>@PREFIX@/share/Geant4/data</code>.</p>
<p>Open a <b>new</b> terminal window before using it: the dataset variables are
set by a line added to <code>/etc/zprofile</code>, which existing windows have
already read.</p>
<p>Applications started from the Finder or the Dock get the same variables from
a login agent, which the installer tried to load into the current session. If
Strata still reports missing datasets, log out and back in, or load it by hand
with <code>@PREFIX@/share/Geant4/geant4-setenv-launchd.sh</code>. The installer
log says which of the two happened.</p>
<p>If a download failed, the installation is still usable; run
<code>sudo @PREFIX@/share/Geant4/fetch-datasets.sh</code> to retry just the
datasets that are missing.</p>
<p>To remove everything: <code>sudo @PREFIX@/bin/uninstall-geant4.sh</code></p>
</body></html>
